    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (266 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change is implemented so that creating an owner returns a computed `displayName` field formatted as `'LastName, FirstName'`.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` gains the field. Since it's under the `Owner`-specific properties (not `OwnerFields`), it appears only in responses, not request bodies.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` with an expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes `displayName` as `lastName + \", \" + firstName`. This covers all owner responses (create, get, update, list).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`** \u2014 Extended `createOwnerSuccess` to assert `$.displayName` equals `\"LastName, George\"`, verifying the new behavior.\n\nAll 266 tests pass.",
